.SH "COMMUNICATION"
.SS "GENERAL"
This chapter describes how the VT220 communicates with a hot computer
and a printer.
.P
The terminal operates on full-duplex asynchronous lines only, and has
ten possible transmit/receive speeds. You select the transmit/receive
speeds in set-up for both the terminal (Communications Set-Up screen)
and the printer (Printer Set-Up screen).
.P
The VT220 operates in accordance with the following national and
international communications standards.
.P
.RS
EIA Standard RS232C/RS423
.br
CCITT V.24
.br
CCITT V.26 (V.10)
.br
CCITT X.20 (V.21)
.RE
.P
You can connect the terminal directly to a local host computer with a
cable. You can also connect the terminal indirectly to a remote host
computer through public-switched or dedicated telephone lines, using a
modem or acoustic coupler.
.
.SS "HOST AND PRINTER PORT INTERFACES"
The VT220 has two asynchronous serial ports. One port is for
communication with a host computer, and the other is for communication
with a printer.
.P
There are two host port connectors.
.bP
A 25-pin subminiature D-type (EIA RS232C/RS423) connector that connects
the terminal to a local or remote host computer.
.bP
An 8-pin EIA Mate-N-Lok (20 mA) connector that connects the terminal to
a local host computer.
.P
The printer port has one connector.
.bP
A 9-pin subminiature D-type (EIA RS232C/RS423) connector that connects
the terminal to a local printer.
.P
Tables 5-1 through 5-3 describe the interface signals for the three
connectors.
.P
.B NOTE:
.B Only the connector pins listed in Tables 5-1 through 5-3 are used.
.
.SS "MODEMS"
The VT220 can operate with all modems conforming to the national and
international standards listed at the beginning of this chapter.
However, the modem at the terminal must be compatible with the modem at
the host computer.
.P
The VT220 accepts compatible modems and acoustic couplers such as the
AT&T 103, 113, and 212 types, in addition to Digital's DF02 and DF03.
.P
The terminal must be certified for connection to non-AT&T type modems
used outside of continental North America. Your local Digital Field
Service office has detailed information on terminal certification and
use of non-AT&T type modems.
.
.TBL "5-1" "Comm Port EIA Interface Signals"
.TS
lBT lBT lBT lBT lBTX
lT lT lT lT lTX.
Pin	Signal	Mnemonic	EIA/CCITT/DIN	Description

2	Transmit data	TXD	BA/103/D1	T{
.I From VT220
.br
Transmits serial characters. Held in mark state when no characters are
transmitted.

In modem control modes, transmits data only when RTS, CTS, DSR, and DTR
are on.
T}

3	Received data	RXD	BB/104/D2	T{
